<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">United Party (South Africa)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1934">1934</a>–<a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The United Party was a South African political party formed in 1934 by the fusion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/j-b-m-hertzog">J. B. M. Hertzog</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-south-africa">National Party</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-smuts">Jan Smuts</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-african-party">South African Party</a>. It governed until 1948, under Hertzog until he left over entry into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> in 1939 and then under Smuts, before losing the election to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/d-f-malan">D. F. Malan</a>'s apartheid platform. It remained the main opposition party until it dissolved in 1977.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-party-south-africa.jpg" alt="United Party (South Africa)" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harris &amp; Ewing, photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_Christiaan_Smuts.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
